h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e0aeb307522526ecc8d3169a452dbd95f353d2f4dc210f52c0e929d0d3901acf","event_uuid":"d3d79649-676a-46e8-bd63-54dd1dc7ec4c","position":{"commit_sha":"d7d939d0e273a3e0c1472f725973b4965f0631cb","position":"1786760029952919001-d3d79649-676a-46e8-bd63-54dd1dc7ec4c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f3c8811c4298ec673dc7a7b35fe6d662ade15d5bad66f4d7705ca1e50a429b4e","event_uuid":"ca2e4e6f-6543-4a5e-a545-3bb26f9030e8","position":{"commit_sha":"180c6117d1511c1580c23289260ef9a669c840cd","position":"1786765186642854001-ca2e4e6f-6543-4a5e-a545-3bb26f9030e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"99b656f13893b5fa68a7cac1ddebcd286f34cbace335027e6fb9ce19c027605a","event_uuid":"57bbbb6c-3336-4b3b-8099-33163e558ab8","position":{"commit_sha":"90f803d0c07b304e7153b82b032c33a0583d4c2e","position":"1786766844228406001-57bbbb6c-3336-4b3b-8099-33163e558ab8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786759964065889001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"56df6082-090e-4b85-abbb-e74b27fc9fa2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8d74-2c9f-c98f-4f0b"},{"link_uuid":"456d9160-944d-42a0-bf4c-209b9f41c536","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01"}],"description":"## Why\nWhen the completion verifier fails a close with \"insufficient evidence\" because the evidence search EXHAUSTED its step budget without refuting any criterion, the correct next action is mechanical: run it again. The verdict cache (Gerrit 1796) banks per-criterion PASSes at finalize even on overall FAIL, so a re-run seeds the credited criteria and spends its whole budget on the formerly-insufficient ones. This was demonstrated live (2026-08-14, ticket deadbeat-warlike-ostrich / 8d74): first close FAILed on exhaustion; an identical re-run closed clean with zero operator-added evidence. Operator ruling: bounded-search exhaustion is the gate's problem to resolve, not the operator's — the gate should auto-resume instead of demanding a human retype the same command.\n\n## Mechanism (maps to existing callables only)\nA resumption is a WHOLE-VERIFIER RE-RUN — exactly what the manual 8d74 re-close did — not a partial continuation. No new verification entry point:\n1. The resumption loop lives at the shared close-gate verification seam — the code that invokes `verify_completion` and inspects its verdict (gate dispatch / CompletionAgentStep caller side) — NOT in the CLI-only close path, so CLI, MCP, and library closes all get it. Executor confirms the exact seam (candidates: the gate_dispatch step that close_precheck's verdict inspection consumes) before coding, and records it in a ticket comment.\n2. Classification: a FAIL qualifies for auto-resume ONLY when (a) at least one criterion is insufficient-evidence/exhausted, and (b) NO criterion was REFUTED (affirmative evidence the work was not done). Any refutation → fail fast, no resume (current behavior). Classification comes from the per-criterion verdict statuses the verifier already returns (completion_failures.py taxonomy); no new telemetry.\n3. On qualification: re-invoke `verify_completion` with the same args/ref. The verdict cache seeds credited PASSes (existing behavior, no change needed); the fresh budget concentrates on remaining criteria (budget derivation unchanged — `verify_step_floor` stays parameterized on the total criteria count; concentration is emergent from cache hits consuming ~0 steps, as observed in the 8d74 live run).\n4. Bounded: `verify.auto_resume_max` resumptions per close invocation, default 2, 0 disables. Each resumption logged to the ticket trail (comment or verdict metadata): attempt number, criteria credited-from-cache count, criteria remaining.\n5. Overall outcome: PASS on any attempt → close proceeds. Still exhausted after the bounded resumptions → the existing failure surface, with the message stating auto-resume was attempted N times (operator sees honest state).\n\n## Out of scope (split to child idea ticket)\nSearch-frontier handoff (steering a resumption away from already-searched places / toward where credited evidence was found) requires an argument-level tool-call transcript the verifier telemetry does not currently carry. That capability question — and the extractor design on top of it — is a separate idea ticket linked discovered_from this one; THIS ticket's resumption passes no frontier and needs no fallback (cache seeding alone proved sufficient live).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Auto-resume triggers only on exhaustion-without-refutation: unit tests cover (a) exhausted+no-refutation → resumes; (b) any refuted criterion → fails fast with no resume; (c) plain PASS → no resume.\n- [ ] Resumption re-invokes the existing `verify_completion` entry (asserted via call-count on the real seam), with the same ref binding (`--ref` closes resume against the same pinned ref).\n- [ ] Bounded by `verify.auto_resume_max` (default 2, 0 disables; config-registry regenerated); attempts beyond the bound surface the existing failure with an attempts-count message (tested).\n- [ ] Resumption trail recorded per attempt (attempt number, cache-credited count, remaining count) and visible on the ticket or in the close output (tested).\n- [ ] The loop sits at the shared gate seam: an MCP-or-library-path close exercises it in a test, not only the CLI path.\n- [ ] Child idea ticket for frontier handoff created + linked discovered_from this ticket before this ticket closes.\n- [ ] `make lint` / `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"CompletionAgentStep orchestration: resumption loop on exhaustion-without-refutation"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_failures.py","reason":"failure taxonomy: classify exhaustion vs refutation outcomes"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_criteria.py","reason":"criteria bounds: per-resumption budget accounting"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py","reason":"credited PASS seeding between resumptions; frontier-digest extractor"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/","reason":"RED-first tests: auto-resume, bounded resumptions, frontier handoff"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b5f8-d3f9-39d9-4195","ticket_type":"task","title":"Close gate auto-resumes verification on search exhaustion instead of failing to the operator","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["420dcd6f-62bf-4c77-9e3f-23ee91f38fd6","56df6082-090e-4b85-abbb-e74b27fc9fa2","456d9160-944d-42a0-bf4c-209b9f41c536","d3d79649-676a-46e8-bd63-54dd1dc7ec4c","ca2e4e6f-6543-4a5e-a545-3bb26f9030e8","57bbbb6c-3336-4b3b-8099-33163e558ab8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786772518978397001,"uuid":"e64cdb8e-09f7-49a4-bd56-bb3e2321418e"}